data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `nint` and `nuint` into a `Span`.** Both of these work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, each element is **8 bytes**. The only gotcha encountered was that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context because the size isn't fixed at compile time — but `stackalloc` itself works fine in safe code when assigned to a `Span`.
